    "body": "### What\n\n`TestCosmosDreamsRuntime::test_overlap_and_serial_vae_inputs_match` calls\n`queue.stream.synchronize()` before `self.assertTrue(queue.stream.query())`.\n\n### Why\n\nThe block under test injects a rollout failure, which cancels in-flight VAE work. The\ntest then asserts the stream is idle. But `Stream.query()` is a non-blocking poll -- it\nreports whether the device has *already* finished, not whether it *will*. The cancelled\nwork is still draining when the poll happens, so `query()` returns `False` at random and\nthe subtest fails with no error message beyond `SUBFAILED(dtype=torch.float32)`.\n\n`synchronize()` blocks until the device actually drains, which is what the assertion\nmeans to check. The assertion itself is kept so the test still fails loudly if the stream\nis somehow non-idle after a full drain.\n\nThis is a test-side race, not a product bug -- no mmgen runtime code is touched.\n\n### Verification -- offline on MI300X (gfx942, ROCm 10.0)\n\nContainer from `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.22-rocm10-mi30x-20261017`, single GPU, **idle card**\n(no competing load), 20 consecutive runs of the single test each way:\n\n| | result |\n|---|---|\n| **Before** | **17 / 20 passed** -- 3 failures, ~15% flake rate |\n| **After** | **20 / 20 passed** |\n\nThe failure is *not* load-dependent: it reproduces on an otherwise idle GPU, which is\nconsistent with a poll/teardown race rather than contention. An A/B under added GPU load\ndid not meaningfully change the rate.\n\n### CI reference\n\n`multimodal-gen-test-1-gpu-amd (rocm10, linux-mi300-1gpu-sglang, 3)`:\n\n```\nSUBFAILED(dtype=torch.float32) sglang/multimodal_gen/test/unit/test_cosmos_dreams.py::TestCosmosDreamsRuntime::test_overlap_and_serial_vae_inputs_match\n= 1 failed, 1112 passed, 17 skipped, 8 deselected, 3 xfailed, 33 warnings, 189 subtests passed =\n```\n\nThis is the only failure in the shard; the other 1112 items pass.\n\n### Note for reviewers\n\nI did not audit the rest of the file for the same pattern. If other tests poll `query()`\nright after a cancellation they will be flaky in the same way, but I only have measured\nevidence for this one, so I kept the change minimal rather than speculatively editing\nsites I have not reproduced.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #39913856012](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39913856012)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39913855695](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39913855695)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39913855972](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39913855972)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
